{
  "id": "ALAS2023-2026-2135",
  "title": "Amazon Linux 2023 - ALAS2023-2026-2135: Important priority package update for samba",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-09-14 09:00:00"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-09-14 14:56:00"
  },
  "severity": "Important",
  "description": "Package updates are available for Amazon Linux 2023 that fix the following vulnerabilities:\nCVE-2026-6949:\n\tTSIG packet with name compression can crash DNS\n\nCVE-2026-58218:\n\tDNS signing DoS via TKEY name cache exhaustion\n\nNOTE: https://www.samba.org/samba/security/CVE-2026-58218-advisory.html\n\nCVE-2026-15779:\n\tA flaw was found in samba's pam_winbind. When mkhomedir is enabled, pam_winbind chowns the target account's home directory without validating the path is not a critical system directory such as /. On affected systems, accounts with / as their home directory (a common default for system accounts) can have this triggered not only by root, but by a non-root user holding a narrow sudo delegation to run commands as that account, causing ownership of / to change and resulting in severe denial of service (SSH, sudo, and package-manager failures). The change does not grant write access to / (which ships with restrictive 0555 permissions on RHEL), so the impact is availability loss rather than further privilege escalation.\n",
